22. Duplicate Startup Refresh Investigation
Current performance instrumentation has demonstrated approximately 16 chart refresh operations in the observed startup scenario even though the dashboard has 8 charts.

This must be investigated before finalizing startup optimization.

Required investigation:

Why are 16 refreshes occurring?

Determine:

Which 8 belong to initial chart creation
Which 8 belong to secondary initialization/update
Whether popup charts are involved
Whether layout restoration triggers another refresh
Whether chart configuration triggers another refresh
Whether duplicate refreshes can be eliminated
The preferred V2 solution is:

eliminate unnecessary duplicate work

rather than merely hiding it behind a cache.

23. Memory Architecture
Memory usage is a first-class V2 concern.

The repository must avoid unnecessary copies of identical contract data.

Bad:

Chart 1 → NIFTY DataFrame A
Chart 2 → NIFTY DataFrame B
Chart 3 → NIFTY DataFrame C

Preferred:

                    NIFTY DataFrame
                         │
             ┌───────────┼───────────┐
             ▼           ▼           ▼
          Chart 1     Chart 2     Chart 3

Derived timeframe data should similarly be shared.

24. Memory Ownership
The architecture must clearly define ownership:

DataRepository
    owns cached data

ChartSlot
    references/consumes data

Browser
    owns rendered chart state

A chart must not independently maintain unnecessary copies of large datasets.

25. Cache Lifecycle
The repository must support:

LOAD
  ↓
CACHE
  ↓
REUSE
  ↓
INVALIDATE
  ↓
RELOAD

Future V2.x versions may add:

LRU eviction
maximum memory limits
explicit contract unloading
background preloading
but these should not be introduced until required.

