30. Contract Change
When a user changes:

Chart 1:
NIFTY → SENSEX

the chart should request:

repository.get("SENSEX", timeframe)

If SENSEX is already cached:

No Excel read
No timeframe recomputation if cached

If not cached:

Load SENSEX
Process requested timeframe
Cache result
Return to chart

31. Timeframe Change
When a user changes:

NIFTY / 1m
       ↓
NIFTY / 5m

the repository checks:

("NIFTY", "5m")

If cached:

return cached result

If not:

use raw NIFTY
    ↓
generate 5m
    ↓
cache
    ↓
return

The workbook must not be reread.

32. Layout Architecture
Layout configuration must remain independent of data storage.

A layout should contain chart configuration such as:

contract
timeframe
chart settings
position
visibility

The layout must not contain duplicated DataFrames.

Conceptually:

Layout
  │
  ├── Chart configuration
  │
  └── references contract/timeframe
             │
             ▼
       DataRepository

33. Popup Architecture
Popup charts must use the same DataRepository as the main dashboard.

They must NOT create an independent data cache.

Example:

Main Dashboard ──────┐
                     │
Popup Charts ────────┼──→ DataRepository
                     │
Other views ─────────┘

If a popup displays:

NIFTY / 1m

while the main dashboard already has:

NIFTY / 1m

the popup must reuse the existing cached data.

34. Error Handling
The repository must provide clear errors for:

Missing worksheet
Invalid contract
Invalid timeframe
Workbook unavailable
Workbook changed while loading
Invalid data
Empty worksheet
Errors must not corrupt existing valid cached data.

35. Threading / Concurrency
The initial V2 implementation should prioritize correctness.

Do not introduce complex threading merely to make Excel loading asynchronous.

First establish:

single authoritative repository
correct caching
duplicate prevention
clear ownership

Background loading can be introduced later if profiling demonstrates startup blocking as a significant issue.

If concurrency is later introduced, duplicate requests for the same cache key must still be coalesced.

36. Architecture Rules
The following rules are mandatory for V2:

Rule 1
ChartSlot must not directly own shared workbook data.

Rule 2
ChartSlot must not directly perform repeated load_sheet() calls.

Rule 3
Raw data cache key:

contract

Rule 4
Processed data cache key:

(contract, timeframe)

Rule 5
Data loading must be lazy.

Rule 6
Identical contract requests must reuse raw data.

Rule 7
Identical contract/timeframe requests must reuse processed data.

Rule 8
Workbook changes must invalidate affected cached data.

Rule 9
Main dashboard and popup charts must share the same repository.

Rule 10
Crosshair synchronization must remain a separate subsystem.

Rule 11
JavaScript call sites must not all be optimized as one problem.

Rule 12
Performance changes must be supported by measurements.

