38. Acceptance Criteria
V2 architecture is considered successful when:

Data loading
The same contract is not repeatedly loaded from Excel while its cache is valid.

Timeframe processing
The same (contract, timeframe) is not repeatedly transformed while its cache is valid.

Multiple charts
Multiple charts can safely consume the same cached dataset.

Multiple contracts
Different workbook sheets work independently.

Multiple timeframes
The same contract can be displayed at different timeframes simultaneously.

Popups
Popup charts share the same data repository.

Workbook changes
Changes to the workbook cause appropriate cache invalidation.

Correctness
Chart output remains identical to the existing implementation for equivalent inputs.

Performance
Performance improvements are demonstrated through measured results rather than assumptions.

Architecture
Future performance optimizations can be implemented without redesigning chart/layout/data ownership.

39. Explicit Non-Goals for Initial V2
The following must NOT be implemented prematurely:

Replacing Pandas
Replacing Excel
Introducing a database
Introducing Redis
Introducing multiprocessing
Introducing complex threading
Rewriting the chart library
Rewriting the entire UI
Replacing JSON with binary transport
Rewriting crosshair and data architecture simultaneously
These may be considered later only if measurements justify them.

